WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:02.370
So who's my guest this week?

00:00:02.370 --> 00:00:05.670
It's the Chief Medical
Advisor to the U.S. President,

00:00:05.670 --> 00:00:08.130
Dr. Anthony Fauci.

00:00:08.130 --> 00:00:10.830
From death threats to Fauci fever.

00:00:10.830 --> 00:00:12.420
If you become one of the biggest figures

00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:14.100
of the coronavirus pandemic,

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:16.293
you're going to elicit a reaction.

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:19.890
As a member of the White
House COVID Task Force

00:00:19.890 --> 00:00:23.130
under President Trump,
Dr. Fauci became the face

00:00:23.130 --> 00:00:25.530
of the U.S. scientific response.

00:00:25.530 --> 00:00:29.940
As the crisis continued,
science and politics clashed.

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:31.650
His attempts to understand the virus

00:00:31.650 --> 00:00:33.780
and save lives were welcomed by many,

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:36.603
but derided as authoritarian by others.

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:40.590
Some of his advice led
to chants of fire Fauci,

00:00:40.590 --> 00:00:43.110
a slogan that was retweeted by his boss

00:00:43.110 --> 00:00:46.500
in the Oval Office, but he kept his job.

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:48.420
He says letting the science speak

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:50.700
got him into a little bit of trouble.

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:52.530
So how does he see things now

00:00:52.530 --> 00:00:55.140
as the wave of the pandemic retreats

00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:57.633
and with a new president
in the White House?

00:00:58.470 --> 00:00:59.910
Here's what's coming up.

00:00:59.910 --> 00:01:04.410
I chose this and I accept
the risks, but my family,

00:01:04.410 --> 00:01:07.440
my wife and my children
continually get hassled

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:11.850
and threatened by things
that are really unimaginable.

00:01:11.850 --> 00:01:13.950
Are you relieved you
don't have President Trump

00:01:13.950 --> 00:01:15.210
in that position anymore?

00:01:15.210 --> 00:01:18.930
Back then it made it
very uncomfortable for me

00:01:18.930 --> 00:01:22.890
because I had to frankly disagree publicly

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:24.890
with the president of the United States.

00:01:38.580 --> 00:01:41.070
Dr. Fauci, thank you
so much for joining me.

00:01:41.070 --> 00:01:43.470
And I have to say, I feel like I know you

00:01:43.470 --> 00:01:46.110
because I have seen your face so much

00:01:46.110 --> 00:01:48.810
even here in the UK over
the last couple of years.

00:01:48.810 --> 00:01:51.990
How has it been for you becoming so much

00:01:51.990 --> 00:01:53.220
of a household name?

00:01:53.220 --> 00:01:55.260
Well, I don't really think of it at all

00:01:55.260 --> 00:01:58.680
as being a household name,
more so that we have to get

00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:02.340
the correct evolving,
scientific information out.

00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:06.000
And that, since it's such a moving target,

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:08.850
that really necessitates, you know,

00:02:08.850 --> 00:02:12.450
rather frequent updating
of what the status is,

00:02:12.450 --> 00:02:13.620
both from a public health

00:02:13.620 --> 00:02:15.660
as well as from a scientific standpoint.

00:02:15.660 --> 00:02:18.930
So it's really a very unique situation

00:02:18.930 --> 00:02:21.390
that I and some of my colleagues

00:02:21.390 --> 00:02:23.280
find ourselves in,

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:25.410
is that it's not static.

00:02:25.410 --> 00:02:27.420
And when you have an event that occurs

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:31.050
and you brief either
domestically or internationally

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:32.700
and generally things don't change,

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:35.400
you don't see very much of a person,

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:38.940
but when you have a very
fluid dynamic situation

00:02:38.940 --> 00:02:39.960
that we have right now,

00:02:39.960 --> 00:02:43.860
that really creates an
unprecedented situation

00:02:43.860 --> 00:02:46.620
where I have become very well-known

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:50.160
merely because of the
need to continually update

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:53.790
and brief at both a domestic
and international level.

00:02:53.790 --> 00:02:56.940
I mean, to that point and
I totally take that point

00:02:56.940 --> 00:02:59.100
because of the nature of the situation.

00:02:59.100 --> 00:03:01.320
I imagine at times it's been frightening,

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:02.970
you know, how much it's been changing

00:03:02.970 --> 00:03:05.490
and the reality on people's lives.

00:03:05.490 --> 00:03:07.920
You know, you must have
felt enormous pressure.

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:09.690
And I imagine you're also receiving

00:03:09.690 --> 00:03:11.100
a lot of emails from people.

00:03:11.100 --> 00:03:14.010
A lot of people asking
you what was going on.

00:03:14.010 --> 00:03:15.540
Are you able to look back at that now

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:17.520
and kind of take that in?

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:18.990
No, I still can't take it in

00:03:18.990 --> 00:03:22.560
because it's completely
transformed my life

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:24.330
in so many ways and, you know,

00:03:24.330 --> 00:03:26.430
positive ways and negative ways

00:03:26.430 --> 00:03:30.060
because of the charged nature

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:33.390
and the stress that this outbreak has put

00:03:33.390 --> 00:03:36.810
on my own country and
throughout the world,

00:03:36.810 --> 00:03:40.380
superimposed upon the
divisive political nature

00:03:40.380 --> 00:03:42.690
in my own country.

00:03:42.690 --> 00:03:46.123
There has been really a

00:03:46.123 --> 00:03:49.265
great deal of divisiveness

00:03:49.265 --> 00:03:51.750
and even rancor among people

00:03:51.750 --> 00:03:54.150
so that you have people who look to you.

00:03:54.150 --> 00:03:57.180
Many, many people and I think the majority

00:03:57.180 --> 00:03:59.310
that look to the science look to me

00:03:59.310 --> 00:04:03.210
as someone who is
communicating the science

00:04:03.210 --> 00:04:06.390
and the public health
in a way that's positive

00:04:06.390 --> 00:04:08.790
and productive cause they wanna know

00:04:08.790 --> 00:04:11.250
what's best for themselves
and their family

00:04:11.250 --> 00:04:13.050
and their community.

00:04:13.050 --> 00:04:17.340
And yet there are some, you
know, who really are swept up

00:04:17.340 --> 00:04:21.480
in conspiracy theories
and distortions of reality

00:04:21.480 --> 00:04:26.480
and anti-science untruths
that create a hostility

00:04:26.910 --> 00:04:30.150
towards me and the scientific
community in general

00:04:30.150 --> 00:04:32.820
that really as unprecedented,

00:04:32.820 --> 00:04:35.640
we've never seen anything like that

00:04:35.640 --> 00:04:38.913
where the only thing
that I've ever expressed,

00:04:39.964 --> 00:04:42.780
everything that I've ever communicated

00:04:42.780 --> 00:04:45.330
has been based on the reality

00:04:45.330 --> 00:04:47.310
and the evidence as we know it.

00:04:47.310 --> 00:04:49.740
And it does change the evidence

00:04:49.740 --> 00:04:52.350
because there are things that we know now,

00:04:52.350 --> 00:04:54.930
we're dealing with a virus
that continues to fool us.

00:04:54.930 --> 00:04:56.790
It continues to move.

00:04:56.790 --> 00:04:58.350
It continues to evolve.

00:04:58.350 --> 00:05:01.500
It continues to create new variants.

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:04.350
In your country, what do
you attribute that to,

00:05:04.350 --> 00:05:07.440
that lack of trust amongst some?

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:09.900
Well, it's become the politicization

00:05:09.900 --> 00:05:14.900
of what should be a purely
public health issue.

00:05:14.910 --> 00:05:18.084
The idea that we have in our country,

00:05:18.084 --> 00:05:20.850
the level of acceptance

00:05:20.850 --> 00:05:25.850
of well-proven public health interventions

00:05:26.160 --> 00:05:28.290
such as vaccines,

00:05:28.290 --> 00:05:31.470
which have clearly been
shown to be lifesaving,

00:05:31.470 --> 00:05:35.160
to be highly effective and very safe,

00:05:35.160 --> 00:05:39.300
and very often, it's along ideologic lines

00:05:39.300 --> 00:05:40.140
when it should be.

00:05:40.140 --> 00:05:43.890
There should be no ideological differences

00:05:43.890 --> 00:05:46.980
in interpretation of what our core,

00:05:46.980 --> 00:05:50.160
immutable public health principles.

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:53.100
And yet the pushback that we have

00:05:53.100 --> 00:05:56.190
against seemingly obvious

00:05:56.190 --> 00:05:59.880
and scientifically proven
public health principles

00:05:59.880 --> 00:06:00.870
is extraordinary.

00:06:00.870 --> 00:06:03.030
And the degree of rancor

00:06:03.030 --> 00:06:05.220
is such that I never would've imagined

00:06:05.220 --> 00:06:09.180
in my wildest dreams that
anything that I've ever said

00:06:09.180 --> 00:06:11.010
which is purely public health

00:06:11.010 --> 00:06:13.980
and non-political and non-ideologic

00:06:13.980 --> 00:06:18.000
leads to continual
death threats against me

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:21.060
to the point where I have to be surrounded

00:06:21.060 --> 00:06:25.110
by federal agents for my
protection all the time.

00:06:25.110 --> 00:06:28.020
I mean, that seems inconceivable.

00:06:28.020 --> 00:06:29.610
If you turn back the clock

00:06:29.610 --> 00:06:33.180
and talk about other public health crises

00:06:33.180 --> 00:06:36.300
that we've had with polio and with measles

00:06:36.300 --> 00:06:39.300
and with smallpox and
the things that we've had

00:06:39.300 --> 00:06:41.460
to alert the public to,

00:06:41.460 --> 00:06:42.930
there's never been a situation

00:06:42.930 --> 00:06:45.390
where the divisiveness have led

00:06:45.390 --> 00:06:48.660
to the threat of physical harm.

00:06:48.660 --> 00:06:53.660
That is as unprecedented as the notoriety

00:06:53.820 --> 00:06:58.470
that I have regarding
the purely communication

00:06:58.470 --> 00:06:59.970
of public health principles.

00:06:59.970 --> 00:07:01.710
How did you cope with that?

00:07:01.710 --> 00:07:04.650
How have you coped with
having death threats?

00:07:04.650 --> 00:07:06.030
I mean, are you scared?

00:07:06.030 --> 00:07:07.653
What about your family as well?

00:07:08.880 --> 00:07:11.370
Well, you know, I mean, I have a job

00:07:11.370 --> 00:07:13.380
and I've devoted myself to my job.

00:07:13.380 --> 00:07:16.800
I've been at the NIH now
for more than 50 years

00:07:16.800 --> 00:07:20.400
and I've been the
director of the Institute,

00:07:20.400 --> 00:07:21.900
the National Institute of Allergy

00:07:21.900 --> 00:07:25.230
and Infectious Diseases for 38 years

00:07:25.230 --> 00:07:27.990
and I've served and
advised seven presidents,

00:07:27.990 --> 00:07:30.810
going all the way back to Ronald Reagan.

00:07:30.810 --> 00:07:32.040
So this is my job.

00:07:32.040 --> 00:07:33.120
I understand it.

00:07:33.120 --> 00:07:35.910
And this is the life that I've chosen.

00:07:35.910 --> 00:07:39.420
I never would've imagined
that it would be beset

00:07:39.420 --> 00:07:42.210
with the kinds of rancor and threats.

00:07:42.210 --> 00:07:43.260
So I don't like it.

00:07:43.260 --> 00:07:45.183
My family, I think, is the one

00:07:45.183 --> 00:07:50.183
that I feel more concerned about because

00:07:50.350 --> 00:07:52.260
I chose this

00:07:52.260 --> 00:07:55.620
and I accept the risks, but my family,

00:07:55.620 --> 00:07:58.650
my wife and my children
continually get hassled

00:07:58.650 --> 00:08:02.910
and threatened by things
that are really unimaginable.

00:08:02.910 --> 00:08:05.250
I mean, obscene phone calls and threats

00:08:05.250 --> 00:08:08.220
and knowing their addresses
and knowing where they work

00:08:08.220 --> 00:08:12.600
and knowing what they do and
to continually hassling them.

00:08:12.600 --> 00:08:16.110
That is just absolutely preposterous

00:08:16.110 --> 00:08:18.570
that that goes on in societies.

00:08:18.570 --> 00:08:20.010
I'm very sorry to hear that.

00:08:20.010 --> 00:08:22.470
You know, I really am because, of course,

00:08:22.470 --> 00:08:24.240
what you're doing at
the same time, you know,

00:08:24.240 --> 00:08:25.290
you're trying to save lives

00:08:25.290 --> 00:08:28.080
and yet you're receiving death threats.

00:08:28.080 --> 00:08:30.540
I understand it's different
to what has been before,

00:08:30.540 --> 00:08:33.120
but who do you blame for that?

00:08:33.120 --> 00:08:34.440
You know, I don't think

00:08:34.440 --> 00:08:36.990
that one can just pick out a person

00:08:36.990 --> 00:08:41.520
or a movement to blame,
but what we do have

00:08:41.520 --> 00:08:45.120
is something that's very
disturbing in this country,

00:08:45.120 --> 00:08:49.800
is what I refer to as the
normalization of untruths.

00:08:49.800 --> 00:08:53.220
There's so much distortion of reality

00:08:53.220 --> 00:08:57.810
and conspiracy theories
that are spread widely

00:08:57.810 --> 00:09:00.330
by social media, where you know,

00:09:00.330 --> 00:09:03.300
social media can have a
positive impact on society

00:09:03.300 --> 00:09:07.470
by spreading important
productive information.

00:09:07.470 --> 00:09:12.470
But when you get total
untruths and quite frankly,

00:09:12.870 --> 00:09:17.870
lies and absolute crazy
distortions of reality

00:09:18.510 --> 00:09:22.260
that get picked up, spread
through the social media,

00:09:22.260 --> 00:09:25.770
and then certain elements
in our own political system

00:09:25.770 --> 00:09:28.980
utilize that to distort reality.

00:09:28.980 --> 00:09:33.180
And it just compounds the
divisiveness in the country.

00:09:33.180 --> 00:09:35.460
When you talk about elements
in the political society,

00:09:35.460 --> 00:09:37.680
obviously I was looking back at your time

00:09:37.680 --> 00:09:38.910
and what was said certainly

00:09:38.910 --> 00:09:40.740
under the previous
president, President Trump,

00:09:40.740 --> 00:09:42.360
and reminding myself of the time

00:09:42.360 --> 00:09:44.370
he suggested injecting disinfectant

00:09:44.370 --> 00:09:47.367
to clean COVID out of the body.

00:09:47.367 --> 00:09:49.710
Are you relieved you
don't have President Trump

00:09:49.710 --> 00:09:50.880
in that position anymore?

00:09:50.880 --> 00:09:54.660
Back then it made it
very uncomfortable for me

00:09:54.660 --> 00:09:58.920
because in order to
maintain my own integrity

00:09:58.920 --> 00:10:01.800
as well as to fulfill my responsibility

00:10:01.800 --> 00:10:03.690
to the American public,

00:10:03.690 --> 00:10:07.290
I had to frankly disagree publicly

00:10:07.290 --> 00:10:09.030
with the president of the United States.

00:10:09.030 --> 00:10:10.950
And that is a very difficult thing to do.

00:10:10.950 --> 00:10:12.930
I did not enjoy that,

00:10:12.930 --> 00:10:17.700
but that created a backlash against me

00:10:17.700 --> 00:10:22.380
by people who were staunchly
loyal to the president.

00:10:22.380 --> 00:10:25.590
Can I ask about the America,
whether it's, the U.S.,

00:10:25.590 --> 00:10:29.190
whether it's out of the
pandemic phase of COVID,

00:10:29.190 --> 00:10:30.630
where are you at with that?

00:10:30.630 --> 00:10:33.900
Well, you know, I think
that leads to confusion

00:10:33.900 --> 00:10:37.530
because understandably
you would not expect

00:10:37.530 --> 00:10:41.670
the general public to appreciate
all the different nuances.

00:10:41.670 --> 00:10:45.810
If you talk about the
explosive phase of a pandemic

00:10:45.810 --> 00:10:47.670
where you have no countermeasures,

00:10:47.670 --> 00:10:50.370
you have no vaccines, you have no drugs.

00:10:50.370 --> 00:10:54.240
I mean, thankfully, the number of deaths

00:10:54.240 --> 00:10:57.570
and hospitalizations as a ratio

00:10:57.570 --> 00:11:01.320
compared to the number
of cases is much lower.

00:11:01.320 --> 00:11:04.590
We're having considerable
number of cases now

00:11:04.590 --> 00:11:07.560
in the U.S. as we get new and new,

00:11:07.560 --> 00:11:10.140
more variants as they evolve.

00:11:10.140 --> 00:11:14.640
The deaths are still at
a high level, 300 a day,

00:11:14.640 --> 00:11:17.700
but it's not the 3,000 a day

00:11:17.700 --> 00:11:20.160
that we were having several months ago.

00:11:20.160 --> 00:11:22.260
So, you know, everything is relative.

00:11:22.260 --> 00:11:23.760
Are we still in a pandemic?

00:11:23.760 --> 00:11:25.650
Absolutely, we are.

00:11:25.650 --> 00:11:28.050
Are we in that very fulminant stage

00:11:28.050 --> 00:11:30.180
that we were in last year?

00:11:30.180 --> 00:11:32.935
No, and hopefully, the more people

00:11:32.935 --> 00:11:35.250
that get vaccinated and boosted

00:11:35.250 --> 00:11:38.190
and the more people who
realize the importance

00:11:38.190 --> 00:11:41.310
of when you have a high
level of viral dynamics,

00:11:41.310 --> 00:11:43.740
that when you're in an indoor setting,

00:11:43.740 --> 00:11:47.850
you should wear a mask,
even though the whole world

00:11:47.850 --> 00:11:50.610
including the United States and the UK

00:11:50.610 --> 00:11:54.510
are just worn out and
tired by this outbreak.

00:11:54.510 --> 00:11:55.890
It isn't over yet.

00:11:55.890 --> 00:12:00.060
People need to realize it is
never gonna go back to zero.

00:12:00.060 --> 00:12:02.610
That's not the nature of this virus.

00:12:02.610 --> 00:12:04.920
What do you make of those
who talk about the fact

00:12:04.920 --> 00:12:08.400
that now the media aren't
doing those daily counts

00:12:08.400 --> 00:12:10.710
and it isn't being covered, if you like,

00:12:10.710 --> 00:12:13.053
in the same way that, you know,

00:12:14.140 --> 00:12:17.190
it was never as bad as it seemed,

00:12:17.190 --> 00:12:18.023
if you see what you mean.

00:12:18.023 --> 00:12:18.856
So that's not talking about people

00:12:18.856 --> 00:12:19.800
who are conspiracy theorists.

00:12:19.800 --> 00:12:22.290
I'm talking about those
who say it was hyped

00:12:22.290 --> 00:12:24.630
and being hyped and fear was being stoked

00:12:24.630 --> 00:12:26.130
by having that level of coverage.

00:12:26.130 --> 00:12:29.370
Well, first of all, to say it was hyped

00:12:29.370 --> 00:12:32.460
is just completely contradicted

00:12:32.460 --> 00:12:36.120
by the terrible burden
that the entire world,

00:12:36.120 --> 00:12:39.930
including the UK and
certainly the United States,

00:12:39.930 --> 00:12:43.500
we have over 1 million deaths

00:12:43.500 --> 00:12:46.200
in the United States from this outbreak.

00:12:46.200 --> 00:12:47.850
That's not hype.

00:12:47.850 --> 00:12:51.780
That's very painful, stark reality.

00:12:51.780 --> 00:12:54.630
So anybody says that
this has been hyped up

00:12:54.630 --> 00:12:58.170
is just not looking at
what's going on in the world

00:12:58.170 --> 00:13:00.270
and certainly not in the United States.

00:13:00.270 --> 00:13:03.510
And the other part of this, part of COVID

00:13:03.510 --> 00:13:04.860
is long COVID as well.

00:13:04.860 --> 00:13:07.290
People living with the effects of it.

00:13:07.290 --> 00:13:09.750
And I wonder, Dr. Fauci,
what was your take on that?

00:13:09.750 --> 00:13:11.760
How you would actually define it

00:13:11.760 --> 00:13:13.990
'cause there's debates going on

00:13:13.990 --> 00:13:17.460
about how it should be
treated as a physical issue,

00:13:17.460 --> 00:13:19.440
a psychological issue, as both.

00:13:19.440 --> 00:13:20.523
What would you say?

00:13:21.390 --> 00:13:23.820
Well, certainly, it's a real phenomenon.

00:13:23.820 --> 00:13:26.160
I mean, there's always
psychological stress

00:13:26.160 --> 00:13:28.380
associated with disease,

00:13:28.380 --> 00:13:32.070
but I think if you put
that aside for a moment,

00:13:32.070 --> 00:13:34.710
the idea that there's a certain percentage

00:13:34.710 --> 00:13:36.810
of people and it really varies, you know,

00:13:36.810 --> 00:13:41.400
from a few percent, 5%
up to 20 or more percent,

00:13:41.400 --> 00:13:45.210
of individuals who when they get COVID

00:13:45.210 --> 00:13:49.050
and apparently recover
from the acute phase of it

00:13:49.050 --> 00:13:52.200
and they are no longer viral positive,

00:13:52.200 --> 00:13:54.690
if you wanna use that terminology,

00:13:54.690 --> 00:13:58.410
that they have the lingering of symptoms

00:13:58.410 --> 00:14:00.390
that are not fully explainable

00:14:00.390 --> 00:14:05.390
by any yet identifiable
pathogenic process.

00:14:05.550 --> 00:14:08.280
We're working very hard to
try and figure out what it is,

00:14:08.280 --> 00:14:13.080
but the symptom complex has
some degree of consistency.

00:14:13.080 --> 00:14:17.040
The most dominating
one is profound fatigue

00:14:17.040 --> 00:14:18.750
upon minimal exertion.

00:14:18.750 --> 00:14:21.960
Something that would
not fatigue you at all

00:14:21.960 --> 00:14:25.590
in your prior pre-COVID condition.

00:14:25.590 --> 00:14:28.140
People are totally exhausted.

00:14:28.140 --> 00:14:30.330
Sometimes, they have very strange things

00:14:30.330 --> 00:14:32.550
like sleep disturbances,

00:14:32.550 --> 00:14:36.810
like the dysregulation
of body temperatures.

00:14:36.810 --> 00:14:39.420
And some of them have a very strange

00:14:39.420 --> 00:14:42.960
unexplainable difficulty in
focusing or concentrating,

00:14:42.960 --> 00:14:45.817
which is referred to as brain fog.

00:14:45.817 --> 00:14:47.760
Well, it sounds hellish.

00:14:47.760 --> 00:14:49.230
It sounds awful.

00:14:49.230 --> 00:14:50.063
Oh, it is.

00:14:50.063 --> 00:14:51.330
It is and it's real.

00:14:51.330 --> 00:14:53.490
And that's one of the reasons

00:14:53.490 --> 00:14:55.350
why we are concerned about that

00:14:55.350 --> 00:14:58.920
and why we're investigating
it so intensively.

00:14:58.920 --> 00:15:02.670
So long COVID is something
we need to take seriously

00:15:02.670 --> 00:15:05.550
until we find out exactly what it is.

00:15:05.550 --> 00:15:09.300
And quite frankly, you have to
be perfectly honest to admit

00:15:09.300 --> 00:15:12.690
it is unclear exactly what the mechanism

00:15:12.690 --> 00:15:15.120
of this particular condition is.

00:15:15.120 --> 00:15:17.790
If I may just take you to another area

00:15:17.790 --> 00:15:20.070
of concern at the moment, while
I have some time with you,

00:15:20.070 --> 00:15:23.160
there is a lot of concern about monkeypox.

00:15:23.160 --> 00:15:26.910
And I wonder what your level of worry

00:15:26.910 --> 00:15:29.610
about that is with regards to America

00:15:29.610 --> 00:15:33.720
or what you can say about the
current thinking on monkeypox.

00:15:33.720 --> 00:15:36.270
Well, I mean, obviously in a world,

00:15:36.270 --> 00:15:40.650
a global community that's
been beset with COVID

00:15:40.650 --> 00:15:43.800
for two and a half years
and you have yet, again,

00:15:43.800 --> 00:15:48.690
another disease that is
now afflicting people,

00:15:48.690 --> 00:15:52.830
you've gotta make sure that
A, you don't underplay it

00:15:52.830 --> 00:15:56.850
and just brush it aside nor create panic.

00:15:56.850 --> 00:16:00.030
There are some significant
differences here

00:16:00.030 --> 00:16:02.310
because we've known about monkeypox

00:16:02.310 --> 00:16:04.110
for a very long period of time.

00:16:04.110 --> 00:16:07.800
It's been endemic in certain countries,

00:16:07.800 --> 00:16:12.800
particularly in Central and
West Africa for some time.

00:16:12.840 --> 00:16:16.860
By introducing it into
the human population

00:16:16.860 --> 00:16:19.770
in non-endemic areas and it looks like,

00:16:19.770 --> 00:16:22.530
at least from an
epidemiological standpoint,

00:16:22.530 --> 00:16:24.780
that there's a heavy predominance

00:16:24.780 --> 00:16:27.390
among the gay community, gay men,

00:16:27.390 --> 00:16:28.710
men who have sex with men

00:16:28.710 --> 00:16:33.710
because of the close personal
contact that one has.

00:16:34.530 --> 00:16:37.110
It's not necessarily in the true sense

00:16:37.110 --> 00:16:39.240
and we don't know that,
but it's not necessarily

00:16:39.240 --> 00:16:42.450
in the true sense sexually transmitted

00:16:42.450 --> 00:16:46.290
but it appears to be transmitted
among sexual partners

00:16:46.290 --> 00:16:49.860
in the gay men who have
sex with men population.

00:16:49.860 --> 00:16:53.370
I mean, the UNAIDS agency
said at the end of May

00:16:53.370 --> 00:16:55.110
that monkeypox, regarding monkeypox,

00:16:55.110 --> 00:16:57.390
racist and homophobic rhetoric

00:16:57.390 --> 00:16:59.580
risks stigmatizing the disease

00:16:59.580 --> 00:17:01.590
and undermining the response.

00:17:01.590 --> 00:17:03.480
Dr. Fauci, of course,
you built your career

00:17:03.480 --> 00:17:05.550
during the AIDS crisis.

00:17:05.550 --> 00:17:09.570
You'll be very familiar with
the risk around stigmatization.

00:17:09.570 --> 00:17:13.050
And of course, lessons being
learned from COVID, we hope.

00:17:13.050 --> 00:17:16.590
What is your concern or response to that?

00:17:16.590 --> 00:17:20.880
Well, I absolutely believe
we've gotta put aside stigma.

00:17:20.880 --> 00:17:24.420
There should be no
stigmatization associated

00:17:24.420 --> 00:17:28.710
with any subgroup of a
population that has a disease.

00:17:28.710 --> 00:17:32.250
So we've gotta strike the delicate balance

00:17:32.250 --> 00:17:34.740
of making sure the people who we see

00:17:34.740 --> 00:17:37.500
with the evidence appear to be those.

00:17:37.500 --> 00:17:40.950
If you look at a group of 2015 people,

00:17:40.950 --> 00:17:43.500
the majority of them at
least in the United States

00:17:43.500 --> 00:17:46.290
are men who have sex with men.

00:17:46.290 --> 00:17:48.240
That should not be a stigmatization,

00:17:48.240 --> 00:17:50.190
but that should be a clue to help us

00:17:50.190 --> 00:17:52.770
to figure out what's going on right now.

00:17:52.770 --> 00:17:55.860
So we've gotta balance
doing the right thing

00:17:55.860 --> 00:17:59.700
to alert the appropriate
populations and subgroups,

00:17:59.700 --> 00:18:02.940
at the same time as we
don't stigmatize them

00:18:02.940 --> 00:18:07.620
because stigma is the enemy of
good public health practices.

00:18:07.620 --> 00:18:09.690
We've gotta stay away from that

00:18:09.690 --> 00:18:11.310
and do what's right for people

00:18:11.310 --> 00:18:13.560
who are at risk for this infection.

00:18:13.560 --> 00:18:16.770
I suppose it's just, again,
in the era of social media

00:18:16.770 --> 00:18:20.130
and how people like yourself,
public officials like you

00:18:20.130 --> 00:18:22.350
can try and get through when we talked

00:18:22.350 --> 00:18:26.280
about that atmosphere that
that information lives in now.

00:18:26.280 --> 00:18:28.590
Yeah, I mean, social media, again,

00:18:28.590 --> 00:18:32.300
is something that, as
I've said so many times

00:18:32.300 --> 00:18:37.110
in in other settings, there's
a good positive aspect of it

00:18:37.110 --> 00:18:40.050
that you can get good
information circulated

00:18:40.050 --> 00:18:45.050
rapidly and widely, but
it is also a great danger

00:18:45.120 --> 00:18:46.620
when you get things that are put

00:18:46.620 --> 00:18:49.170
into the social media sphere

00:18:49.170 --> 00:18:51.840
and you wind up spreading not only stigma

00:18:51.840 --> 00:18:55.830
and prejudice, but also
counterproductive information.

00:18:55.830 --> 00:18:57.300
So we've gotta be very careful.

00:18:57.300 --> 00:18:58.770
Would you say social media companies

00:18:58.770 --> 00:19:01.080
having allowed that to
happen in certain instances

00:19:01.080 --> 00:19:03.660
pose a public health issue?

00:19:03.660 --> 00:19:06.510
You know, I get asked that question often.

00:19:06.510 --> 00:19:11.510
I am not very well-tuned into what can

00:19:11.760 --> 00:19:15.630
and cannot be done in
regulating disinformation

00:19:15.630 --> 00:19:16.830
and misinformation.

00:19:16.830 --> 00:19:18.870
That's not my lane.

00:19:18.870 --> 00:19:22.440
And I've learned now after
many years of experience,

00:19:22.440 --> 00:19:25.050
don't make proclamations in areas

00:19:25.050 --> 00:19:27.540
that are not my area of expertise.

00:19:27.540 --> 00:19:31.350
So I'm not sure what the
best way to control that.

00:19:31.350 --> 00:19:34.320
There is one productive way to do it,

00:19:34.320 --> 00:19:37.890
is to try and counter misinformation

00:19:37.890 --> 00:19:41.130
and disinformation by getting out there

00:19:41.130 --> 00:19:44.760
and proactively putting out correct,

00:19:44.760 --> 00:19:48.720
scientifically-based, and
sound correct information.

00:19:48.720 --> 00:19:51.390
Well, I mean, I'm also just
minded to bring up the fact

00:19:51.390 --> 00:19:53.430
that you've called gun violence in America

00:19:53.430 --> 00:19:54.600
a public health issue.

00:19:54.600 --> 00:19:57.360
Of course, the debate
about that rages both off

00:19:57.360 --> 00:19:59.340
and online as well.

00:19:59.340 --> 00:20:01.890
And I wonder, is that cutting through?

00:20:01.890 --> 00:20:03.750
Do you think it is finally cutting through

00:20:03.750 --> 00:20:04.830
in any way in America?

00:20:04.830 --> 00:20:08.820
Can you see the political
divide closing any time soon?

00:20:08.820 --> 00:20:11.010
The political divide closing?

00:20:11.010 --> 00:20:15.000
No, I see as we approach
a very important election

00:20:15.000 --> 00:20:17.250
in the United States
that the political divide

00:20:17.250 --> 00:20:19.470
is gonna get even more intense.

00:20:19.470 --> 00:20:22.620
You know, one would hope and
I do hope as a physician,

00:20:22.620 --> 00:20:25.260
a scientist, and a public health official,

00:20:25.260 --> 00:20:28.260
that when you're facing a common enemy,

00:20:28.260 --> 00:20:32.010
that that's the time for a
country to pull together.

00:20:32.010 --> 00:20:34.740
You know, the way you pull together

00:20:34.740 --> 00:20:37.830
after the anthrax attack on our country.

00:20:37.830 --> 00:20:41.760
The way you pull together
after a natural disaster.

00:20:41.760 --> 00:20:46.020
The way the UK pulled
together during World War II.

00:20:46.020 --> 00:20:49.650
And the way we ourselves pulled
together during conflicts.

00:20:49.650 --> 00:20:52.230
But unfortunately, we're not seeing that.

00:20:52.230 --> 00:20:53.670
We're seeing just the opposite.

00:20:53.670 --> 00:20:55.890
We're seeing what should be something

00:20:55.890 --> 00:20:58.170
that brings a nation together,

00:20:58.170 --> 00:21:00.690
is something that's
actually, unfortunately

00:21:00.690 --> 00:21:04.200
and paradoxically having
the opposite effect

00:21:04.200 --> 00:21:06.030
of splitting us up even more.

00:21:06.030 --> 00:21:07.890
The other disease as it were,

00:21:07.890 --> 00:21:09.708
was Fauci fever, I'm told,

00:21:09.708 --> 00:21:11.140
that swept the country.

00:21:12.540 --> 00:21:14.340
Well, your face has been,
I've been told also,

00:21:14.340 --> 00:21:16.170
on things like donuts, all sorts.

00:21:16.170 --> 00:21:18.660
What's the weirdest thing
you've seen your face on?

00:21:18.660 --> 00:21:21.900
And have you been bought
any of the merchandise?

00:21:21.900 --> 00:21:22.983
No, I have not.

00:21:24.930 --> 00:21:26.850
I've been given some of the merchandise.

00:21:26.850 --> 00:21:29.160
I certainly have not bought it.

00:21:29.160 --> 00:21:31.410
Well, have you got a mug, T-shirt?

00:21:31.410 --> 00:21:33.600
Well, you know, these
candles that come out

00:21:33.600 --> 00:21:36.090
are kind of the more extraordinary.

00:21:36.090 --> 00:21:39.541
I mean, I can't imagine I
have my face on a candle.

00:21:39.541 --> 00:21:41.960
That's really way out there.

00:21:41.960 --> 00:21:42.793
That's way out.

00:21:42.793 --> 00:21:44.820
And Brad Pitt apparently played you

00:21:44.820 --> 00:21:45.990
on "Saturday Night Live".

00:21:45.990 --> 00:21:47.463
Yeah, I know.

00:21:48.570 --> 00:21:51.930
You know, most people don't
really appreciate that.

00:21:51.930 --> 00:21:54.240
I can't really pay attention to that

00:21:54.240 --> 00:21:56.807
because I cannot be distracted

00:21:56.807 --> 00:21:58.110
No, I know, I know.
from what I do

00:21:58.110 --> 00:21:59.218
on a daily basis.

00:21:59.218 --> 00:22:00.077
But if you had to pick
someone to play you,

00:22:00.077 --> 00:22:02.010
that's a pretty good one, right?

